---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Roamglyph">
  <strong>Privacy Policy</strong>
  <p>
    This privacy policy applies to the Roamglyph mobile application (the
    "Application"), provided by Bayajit Mohammed (the "Service Provider"). It
    explains what information the Application handles, why it is used, and the
    choices available to you.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Summary</strong>
  <p>
    Roamglyph is a local-first route journal. The Service Provider does not
    operate an account system or server for your routes, annotations, or photos,
    and does not use advertising or analytics SDKs. Your journal data stays on
    your device unless you choose to export it. The Application connects to
    OpenStreetMap to load map tiles, as described below.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Information the Application Handles</strong>
  <p>The Application may handle the following information on your device:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Precise location and timestamps used to show your position, record a
      route, place annotations, and help you retrace a saved route
    </li>
    <li>
      Background location while a recording session is active, so recording
      can continue when the Application is not on screen
    </li>
    <li>
      Route details such as the selected travel mode, session name, distance,
      elapsed time, interruptions, and start and completion times
    </li>
    <li>
      Markers, written comments, and photos that you choose to attach to map
      locations
    </li>
    <li>
      Battery level readings used to show battery information for a recording
      session
    </li>
    <li>
      Device heading used to orient the map when you enable heading-up mode;
      heading is used for display and is not saved in your journal
    </li>
    <li>
      Application preferences and cached map tiles needed to provide the
      features you select
    </li>
  </ul>

  <br />

  <strong>Permissions</strong>
  <p>
    Roamglyph requests precise and background location permissions for route
    recording. On supported Android versions, it also requests notification
    permission so it can display the persistent notification required for
    background recording. Camera or photo-library access is requested only when
    you choose to attach a photo. You can manage these permissions in your
    device settings, although disabling a permission may prevent the related
    feature from working.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Local Storage and Photos</strong>
  <p>
    Routes, annotations, preferences, and attached-photo copies are stored in
    the Application's private storage on your device. When you attach a photo,
    Roamglyph creates a newly encoded copy with EXIF metadata removed and does
    not modify the original image. Cached OpenStreetMap tiles are also stored
    locally and can be cleared from the Application's settings.
  </p>

  <p>
    Local data remains until you delete it through the Application, clear the
    Application's data, or uninstall the Application, subject to any backup or
    restore features provided by your device or operating system.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Exports and Sharing</strong>
  <p>
    If you choose to export a session, Roamglyph creates a JSON file and passes
    it to the Android system share sheet. The export may contain the recorded
    path, timestamps, session details, markers, written comments, and photo
    records. It does not include photo image files or device-local photo paths.
    The destination you select receives the exported data and handles it under
    its own privacy practices. The Service Provider does not receive a copy.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>OpenStreetMap</strong>
  <p>
    Roamglyph requests map images from the OpenStreetMap Foundation's tile
    service when a map area is not available in the local cache or needs to be
    refreshed. Those requests disclose network and request information to the
    OpenStreetMap Foundation, including your IP address, application and device
    information, request time, and the requested tile. A requested tile
    identifies an area of the map you viewed and may correspond to your current
    location. Roamglyph does not send your saved routes, annotations, written
    comments, or photos with these requests.
  </p>
  <p>
    The OpenStreetMap Foundation handles this information under its own
    <a
      href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a
    >. Its map tiles may be served through a global network of cache servers.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Information the Service Provider Does Not Collect</strong>
  <p>
    The Service Provider does not collect your journal data through Roamglyph,
    does not require an account, and does not use the Application to sell or
    share personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising. The
    Application does not include third-party advertising, analytics, or crash
    reporting SDKs.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Your Choices and Rights</strong>
  <p>
    You control the journal data stored by the Application. You can delete
    sessions and annotations in Roamglyph, clear cached map tiles in settings,
    revoke permissions in device settings, or remove local Application data by
    clearing its data or uninstalling it. Once you share an export, you must
    manage that copy with the destination you selected.
  </p>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may also have legal rights concerning
    personal information held by the Service Provider, such as rights to access,
    correct, or delete it. Because Roamglyph does not transmit your journal to
    the Service Provider, the Service Provider generally cannot access or delete
    that local data for you. For privacy requests concerning information you
    send directly to the Service Provider, use the contact details below.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Children's Privacy</strong>
  <p>
    The Application is not directed to children under 13, and the Service
    Provider does not knowingly collect personal information from children
    through the Application. If you believe a child has sent personal
    information directly to the Service Provider, please use the contact details
    below.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Security</strong>
  <p>
    Roamglyph uses private Application storage intended to keep its files
    separate from other applications. No method of storage or transmission is
    completely secure, so absolute security cannot be guaranteed. Protect your
    device and review the destination carefully before sharing an export.
  </p>

  <br />

  <strong>Changes to This Policy</strong>
  <p>
    The Service Provider may update this policy to reflect changes to the
    Application or legal requirements. The updated policy will be posted on
    this page with a revised effective date.
  </p>

  <br />

  <p>This privacy policy is effective as of 2026-09-29.</p>

  <br />

  <strong>Contact Us</strong>
  <p>
    If you have questions or a privacy request, contact the Service Provider at
    <a href="mailto:bayajitmohammed@gmail.com"
      >bayajitmohammed@gmail.com</a
    >.
  </p>
</Layout>
